      "items": [
        {
          "info": {
            "name": "Send Intake Questionnaire",
            "type": "http"
          },
          "http": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/intake_questionnaires/send",
            "body": {
              "type": "json",
              "data": "{}"
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "token": "{{bearerToken}}"
            }
          },
          "docs": "Create an intake questionnaire for the (provider, client) pair.\n\nCallers without an overriding role may only send a questionnaire for themselves\n(403 when ``provider_id`` is someone else's) — the target provider is taken from the\nrequest body, so this prevents a holder of ``post:intake_questionnaires:send`` from\ncreating questionnaires for arbitrary (provider, client) pairs.\n\n400 when the provider is not a practicing guardian for the client, the provider's\nonboarding questionnaire is not COMPLET"
        },
        {
          "info": {
            "name": "List Intake Questionnaires",
            "type": "http"
          },
          "http": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/intake_questionnaires",
            "params": [
              {
                "name": "provider_id",
                "value": "",
                "type": "query",
                "description": "Filter by provider id (must be > 0)."
              },
              {
                "name": "client_id",
                "value": "",
                "type": "query",
                "description": "Filter by client id (must be > 0)."
              },
              {
                "name": "date_start",
                "value": "",
                "type": "query",
                "description": "Only include questionnaires with date_sent on/after this date."
              },
              {
                "name": "date_end",
                "value": "",
                "type": "query",
                "description": "Only include questionnaires with date_sent on/before this date."
              },
              {
                "name": "status",
                "value": "",
                "type": "query",
                "description": "Filter by questionnaire status."
              }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "token": "{{bearerToken}}"
            }
          },
          "docs": "List intake questionnaires (basic columns only, newest date_sent first).\n\nEach returned row also includes a lightweight ``provider`` and ``client`` summary\n(id/name/email) for the linked provider and client.\n\nFilter by ``provider_id``, ``client_id``, ``status``, and a ``date_sent`` window\n(``date_start`` inclusive, ``date_end`` inclusive of the whole day). The window is\npadded by one extra day on each side so records that land on an adjacent UTC day\n(because ``date_sent`` is stored as naive UTC "
        },
        {
          "info": {
            "name": "Get Intake Questionnaires By Provider",
            "type": "http"
          },
          "http": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/intake_questionnaires/by_provider/:provider_id",
            "params": [
              {
                "name": "provider_id",
                "value": "",
                "type": "path",
                "description": "Provider id (must be > 0)"
              },
              {
                "name": "client_id",
                "value": "",
                "type": "query",
                "description": "When set, narrows the result to this provider and client (at most one row). When omitted, returns every questionnaire for the provider."
              }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "token": "{{bearerToken}}"
            }
          },
          "docs": "All intake questionnaires for a provider (basic columns only, newest first).\n\nA provider usually has several clients assigned, so this returns every questionnaire\nat once; pass ``client_id`` to narrow to a single client. Related sections (general\ninfo, medical info, etc.) are omitted.\n\nCallers with broad visibility (an overriding role, or the provider looking up their\nown id) get the real outcome: an empty list when none exists and ``404`` if the\nprovider is missing. Any other caller only sees t"
        },
        {
          "info": {
            "name": "Get Intake Questionnaire By Id",
            "type": "http"
          },
          "http": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/intake_questionnaires/:questionnaire_id",
            "params": [
              {
                "name": "questionnaire_id",
                "value": "",
                "type": "path",
                "description": "Intake questionnaire id (must be > 0)"
              }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "token": "{{bearerToken}}"
            }
          },
          "docs": "Full questionnaire with nested sections; 404 if not found.\n\nCallers without an overriding role may only read questionnaires sent to them (403\notherwise). Sections and collections that have no rows yet (e.g. ``medical_info``,\n``referrals``) are returned as ``null``."
        },
        {
